scrcpy-android
  Source: https://gitlab.com/0xlena/scrcpy-android
  Base commit: 4341eb16f2ff3233599b1f42c91105f424bc016a (0.5)
  License: Apache License 2.0; see scrcpy-android/LICENSE.
  Upstream author: 0xlena and contributors; original notices are retained.
  Local changes include Android compatibility repairs, a phone-shaped virtual
  display, remote application selection, display density controls, rotation,
  immersive controller UI, an edge menu, Chinese resources, and associated tests.
  Paired-device mDNS discovery, GUID-based address refresh, and manual endpoint
  editing preserve existing pairing when wireless-debugging ports change.
  The edge menu uses grouped actions, vector icons and a rounded popup theme.
  Further local changes add a persistent optional navigation overlay, an app
  grid, per-device recent launch history, and ordinary Back key injection
  without the upstream Back-or-screen-on Power fallback.
  Phone-mode virtual system decorations are disabled in favor of the overlay;
  this may also hide the virtual status bar. Main-display mirroring is unchanged.
  A controller menu action sends a dedicated wake-up key to the physical main
  display over ADB, with bounded command reads and execution acknowledgment.
  The client also requests a temporary screen-off timeout during control,
  with restoration handled by the upstream server cleanup process. Compact
  grid controls, recent-history clearing and pairing hints are also local changes.
  Build configuration, embedded server assets and root integration also differ
  from upstream. See PHONE-MODE.md and Git history for details.

